[ ] Map every DSL, charter and objective field to its pattern in the spec =v5-mapping $Rewrite specifications/ontology.md as the mapping, one row per field of actions.schema.json plus charter frontmatter and objective files, each to its pattern in ontology docs/domain.md. Settled already: id is the IRI; name is rdfs:label; state per ontology Decisions 4 and 5, with blocked as waiting on something outside; priority, plus-tag contexts, predecessors and the sequential marker as in the domain table; alias is a Designative Name; description is a Descriptive ICE about the action; parent and children are has continuant part; scheduled and due times are conditions. Still to settle here, by searching for standard terms before any choice: duration; created and completed times (the act and its temporal region); external schedule id and occurrence key (iCal machinery, maybe the W3C RDF Calendar terms); charter lifecycle states; and the workspace facts now in the ws namespace (source file and line, workspace identity), which are not domain meaning and must not be minted if a standard term exists. Also settle the IRIs of the extra nodes V5 needs (conditions, measurements, bearers, acts): deterministic, derived from the action's UUID and the node's role, so exports diff cleanly. Strip the v4 property names from the descriptions in actions.schema.json.$ !1 ^2026-10-01T20:22 #01a0faa2-17cb-77f8-99a0-34646ff8128c
[ ] Write SHACL shapes and a conformance fixture for the V5 output =v5-shapes $Per Decisions 42 and 43, in specifications/schemas beside the JSON schemas: SHACL shapes for the graph the mapping defines, and a fixture, a small workspace with its expected graph, that an implementation must reproduce. Check the fixture with ROBOT too: merged with the ontology it must reason consistent under HermiT. No JSON-LD context as a contract.$ !2 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <01a0faa2-17cb-77f8-99a0-34646ff8128c #01a0faa2-17ea-778f-a8ae-a59285498e28
[ ] Seed the root objective on init and report charters without one =root-objective $Per Decision 43: init writes an objective file and links the root charter to it, once, as it seeds the root alias; doctor reports any charter with no objective, never refusing to load. Spec text in workspace.md and objectives.md, implementation in Core and the CLI. Existing objective files mostly lack frontmatter ids: give them ids in the same pass, as the old charter map asked.$ !2 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <019f5895-6948-70b2-88e2-a7685b0dddda #01a0faa2-1806-7129-814b-f5efdcd6ff41
