[ ] Project workspaces to the V5 graph in Core =v5-projection $The core code change of Decision 43. Replace the v4 projection in clearhead-core rdf/project.rs and rdf/mod.rs with the mapping the spec defines, emitting no v4 terms. Prove it against the spec's fixture and shapes at Core's spec-conformance boundary, as the JSON schema conformance already runs, and check reasoner consistency with the ontology. Expect the graph to grow about tenfold per action; measure load and query time on this workspace before and after.$ !1 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <01a0faa2-17ea-778f-a8ae-a59285498e28 <019f5895-6948-70b2-88e2-a7685b0dddda #01a0faa2-7184-74d1-ae6c-1959f4af7fe3
[ ] Move the saved queries to the V5 graph with unchanged rows =v5-queries $Rewrite every saved query in clearhead-cli src/queries and the CLI's sparql modules against the new graph, plus this workspace's .clearhead/queries/for-human.sparql. Row shapes stay as they are, so nvim and other clients do not change; the existing query tests are the net, so freeze their expected rows before rewriting. The competency queries in ontology v5/queries are the working templates.$ !2 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <01a0faa2-7184-74d1-ae6c-1959f4af7fe3 #01a0faa2-71a3-70a1-91c5-a485dedd4de2
[ ] Retire the v4 vocabulary everywhere =retire-v4 $Remove the v4 namespace constants and fixtures from clearhead-core, the ontology's v4 directory, examples and queries, its pytest suite and pyproject deps, and V4_DESIGN.md; point specifications/ontology.md readers at the ontology's docs/domain.md. Decide then whether clearhead.us keeps serving the v4 vocabulary for anyone holding its IRIs (cool URIs do not change) or drops it with the site.$ !3 ^2026-10-01T20:22 <01a0faa2-71a3-70a1-91c5-a485dedd4de2 #01a0faa2-71c0-7365-9b59-8baa79bf9766
